@startuml usecase-03-planned-scenes
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam wrapWidth 170
title Use case 3 — planned-scenes\n"text model derives PICTURE DESCRIPTIONS ONLY,\nthen ALL of them go as ONE block to the image model\n(IDENTICAL to planned-enblock, different prompt templates)"

actor User
participant "LlmUseCaseRunner\n(env)" as RUN
participant "plannedScenes\n(controller)" as UC
participant "plannedStoryboard\n(shared pipeline)" as PIPE
participant "LlmOrchestratorService" as ORCH
participant "LlmTransportService" as XPORT
participant "Evaluators" as EVAL
participant "LlmPostprocessorService" as POST
participant "ChatService" as SVC
participant "Provider\n(proxy)" as NET

== 1. Dialog picks the use case ==
User -> RUN : count(>1), planning ON,\nNOT singleCall/pure\n+ style, storyboard rules
RUN -> RUN : pickUsecase(vars) → 'planned-scenes'

== 2. Run: env ==
RUN -> RUN : beginOperation('illustrate') → Stop ends the use case
render + plan model resolution\n(contextMessages, anchor, imageExtras)
RUN --> UC : controllerFor('planned-scenes')(env)

== 3. Step 1 — planning (SCENE template) ==
UC -> PIPE : plannedStoryboard(env, templates)\ntemplates = { planning: pictureScenePlanningInstruction,\nrender: oneShotScenesPrompt }
PIPE -> ORCH : completion(plan model, expect:'descriptions')
ORCH -> XPORT : complete()
XPORT -> NET : POST /chat/completions (text)
XPORT --> ORCH : raw
ORCH -> EVAL : evaluateDescriptions(raw)
EVAL --> ORCH : descriptions slot (ok | refused, reason)
ORCH --> PIPE : descriptions[]

== 4. Step 2 — ONE en-block render (scene template) ==
PIPE -> PIPE : prompt = oneShotScenesPrompt(instruction,\ndescriptions, count, storyboardRules)
PIPE -> ORCH : completeImage(request, expect:'images')
ORCH -> XPORT : completeImage()
XPORT -> NET : POST /chat/completions (or /images for image-only models)
XPORT --> ORCH : raw (or thrown TransportError)
ORCH -> EVAL : evaluateImagesResponse(raw)
EVAL --> ORCH : images slot (ok | partial | refused, reason)
ORCH --> PIPE : EvalSlots
note over PIPE, ORCH
  An LLM called to render several pictures returns\nONE picture or NONE (e.g. when it moderates one of\nthem). So a NON-EMPTY batch STOPS the use case\nhere — no per-scene fallback, no reprise.\nThe fallback + reprise below run ONLY when the\nbatch returns NOTHING.
end note

== 5. Step 3 — fallback (only when the batch returned 0) ==
alt batch returned 0 pictures
  PIPE -> PIPE : loop scenes 0..count-1 → renderImage(\nscenePrompt(i)) — each sends ONLY its own\ndescription
  loop i in 0..count-1
    PIPE -> ORCH : completeImage(scene i)
    ORCH --> XPORT : completeImage()
    XPORT -> NET : POST /chat/completions (per scene)
    XPORT --> ORCH : raw
    ORCH -> EVAL : evaluateImagesResponse({raw} or {error, aborted})
    EVAL --> ORCH : scene[i] slot (ok | refused, reason)
    ORCH --> PIPE : scene[i]
  end
  alt a scene is still missing AND >1 succeeded
    PIPE -> PIPE : reprisePrompt = oneShotScenesPrompt(\ninstruction, successfulTexts, realCount)
    PIPE -> ORCH : completeImage(reprise)
    ORCH --> PIPE : reprise images
    note over PIPE
      When the reprise yields >= count the whole set is\nreplaced; otherwise each returned image is merged\ninto a still-missing scene slot.
    end note
  end
end

== 6. Place — IMMEDIATELY as each picture is created ==
PIPE -> POST : storyboard = scenes + images — every picture is
placed on the chapter node AS SOON as it is created\nduring the use case, not only after the whole run
POST -> SVC : editAssistant(chapter, illustration-N + prompt-N /\nrefused-prompt-N) — versioned, on the very node\nillustrate was called for
POST --> RUN : activate(chapter.id)\nalert if partial/empty
note over RUN, POST
  One Stop press ends the use case (isOperationCancelled)\n  — pictures already attached stay on the node, so\n  stopping never loses images created so far.
end note

@enduml